---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="MCP TechTeam — Author & Editorial Process | Made in China Peptide"
  description="MCP TechTeam is the technical editorial team of MCP Biotech, writing about peptide identity, purity, documentation and China sourcing for laboratory buyers."
  canonical="/author/mcp-tech-team/"
>
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'MCP TechTeam' }]} />
    <h1>MCP TechTeam</h1>
    <p class="lead muted">
      MCP TechTeam is the technical editorial group behind Made in China Peptide. We write and
      review the product notes, analytical guides and sourcing frameworks published on this site.
      Made in China Peptide is a trading name of <strong>{site.legalName}</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>What we cover</h2>
    <p>
      Our work sits between the analytical laboratory and the purchasing desk. We read certificates
      of analysis, chromatograms and mass spectra; we compare specifications against the questions a
      laboratory actually asks; and we translate the result into a document request a buyer can send
      to a supplier. The knowledge base covers identity and purity methods, counter-ions and net
      content, stability and handling, packaging and cold chain, customs documentation and supplier
      qualification.
    </p>
    <p>
      The product pages are deliberately narrower than a pharmacology reference. They describe what
      the catalogue item is, how the batch should be characterised, what the format is useful for,
      and where a buyer should stop and ask for more evidence. They are not protocols, dosing guides
      or medical advice.
    </p>

    <h2>How we form a view</h2>
    <p>
      We separate three kinds of statement. A <strong>measured value</strong> belongs to a specific
      lot and must travel with that lot's certificate. A <strong>method statement</strong> describes
      how a result was produced and is only comparable when the method is comparable. An
      <strong>editorial judgement</strong> is our reading of the evidence — for example, that a
      certificate without a batch number is not a batch record, or that two suppliers quoting the
      same purity figure may not be measuring the same thing.
    </p>
    <p>
      When the catalogue does not have a sequence, a lot result or a stability study, we say so
      rather than fill the gap with a plausible number. That is also why some pages are shorter than
      others: the page reflects the evidence available, not a word-count target.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections and contact</h2>
    <p>
      If a sentence on this site is wrong, send the page URL, the exact sentence and the source that
      should be checked to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We will review the
      source and correct the page if the evidence supports it. Do not send confidential formulas or
      personal medical information.
    </p>
    <p class="small muted">
      Publisher: {site.legalName}. Brand: {site.brand}. All products are supplied for laboratory
      research use only, not for human or veterinary use.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
